## Getting started

### Install

We test the code on PyTorch 1.10 +  CUDA 11.3

1. Create a new conda environment
 ```
conda create -n DMFMDehazeNet python=3.8
conda activate DMFMDehazeNet
```

2. Install dependencies
```
conda install pytorch=1.10.2 torchvision torchaudio cudatoolkit=11.3 -c pytorch
pip install -e .
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Down
RESIDE数据集获得网址：https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-ytS_ebiDM6kOjcon7rIbKtKFtb9uZvV?usp=drive_link
Haze4K dataset is available at [Haze4K link](https://pan.baidu.com/s/141MW0YAvjFcydlroQZZizA)(pw：cmmr）
You can download the pretrained models on [Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-ytS_ebiDM6kOjcon7rIbKtKFtb9uZvV?usp=drive_link)


The final file path will be arranged as (please check it carefully)：
```
┬─ save_models
│   ├─ indoor
│   │   ├─ dehazeformer-b.pth
│   │   └─ ... (model name)
│   └─ ... (exp name)
└─ data
    ├─ RESIDE-IN
    │   ├─ train
    │   │   ├─ GT
    │   │   │   └─ ... (image filename)
    │   │   └─ hazy
    │   │       └─ ... (corresponds to the former)
    │   └─ test
    │       └─ ...
    └─ ... (dataset name)
```

### Model Training
You can download our model from [Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-ytS_ebiDM6kOjcon7rIbKtKFtb9uZvV?usp=drive_link)

The final file path will be arranged as (please check it carefully)：

```
data
   |-ITS
      |- ITS.lmdb
   |- ...(dataset name)
```

Train the model on the `ITS` dataset using four cards
```
cd XXX
 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3 tools/dist_train.sh ./my_config/MixDehazeNet_all.py 4
```

Train the model on the `OTS` dataset using one cards
```
cd XXX
python train.py --config '模型路径'
```

